// paideia-as#1305 — Argon2id KDF trait declaration.
//
// Split out of `pdx/crypto.pdx` per paideia-as#1354 so parallel
// authoring of the v0.25-v0.32 crypto waves never collides inside a
// shared source file.
//
// The elaborator's `stdlib_lowering::cryptoops::argon2id` recipe
// routes `Argon2id::derive` through the extern-C thunk
// `paideia_crypto_argon2id_derive` in
// `crates/paideia-as-crypto/src/ffi/argon2id.rs`.
//
// # Consumer contract
//
// Consumers pass parameters as pointers to `#[repr(C)]` structs laid
// out to match `Argon2idParamsC` in the Rust FFI module. All lengths
// are `u64`s and every byte-buffer is a plain `*const u8` / `*mut u8`;
// there is no `.pdx`-side wrapper type.
//
// # Return codes (shared across all crypto FFI thunks)
//
//   0   OK
//  -1   InvalidParam (missing pointer / bad `_reserved` field)
//  -2   InvalidLength (output size mismatch)
//  -4   Primitive-internal failure
//
// Callers MUST branch on the return code; a negative value means the
// output buffer is untouched and no bytes were written.
//
// # Effect discipline
//
// The `crypto` effect names the domain (KDF invocation on caller-
// supplied buffers); the `mem` effect covers the pointer dereferences
// the primitive performs on the parameter blob. A dedicated
// `paideia.crypto` capability gates who may invoke this primitive —
// user-authentication paths in R48 (see `design/user/model.md` §2.1,
// §9.2) hold this cap; a driver in a separate cap domain does not.
//
// # References
//
// - RFC 9106 (Argon2id KDF), §3.1 (parameter ranges), §4 (recommended
//   profiles), §5.3 (canonical test vector).

trait Argon2id {
  // derive(params_ptr, out_ptr, out_len) -> return_code (see above)
  //
  //   RDI  params_ptr    *const Argon2idParamsC
  //   RSI  out_ptr       *mut u8
  //   RDX  out_len       u64
  //   RAX  return code (i64)
  //
  // Reference: paideia_crypto_argon2id_derive in
  //            crates/paideia-as-crypto/src/ffi/argon2id.rs.
  fn derive(params_ptr: u64, out_ptr: u64, out_len: u64) -> i64 !{crypto, mem} @{paideia.crypto};
}
